1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,528
My living room is slowly crushing me beneath three hundred pounds of solid lead furniture.

2
00:00:06,828 --> 00:00:16,188
Every unnecessary sentence spoken out in the city materializes inside my apartment the moment I unlock the door.

3
00:00:16,488 --> 00:00:24,240
Today at work, I argued with my boss for five minutes. Now a massive iron desk blocks my kitchen.

4
00:00:24,540 --> 00:00:32,004
Small talk is a luxury tax I can no longer afford. Yesterday's gossip cost me a concrete pillar.

5
00:00:32,304 --> 00:00:39,000
I tried whispering on the phone. The tiny steel cubes piled on my bed still bruised my ribs.

6
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:46,260
So I stopped talking completely. For weeks, I uttered not a single word to anyone.

7
00:00:46,560 --> 00:00:55,416
Yet tonight, returning home, the floorboards groan under the weight of something entirely new and impossibly massive.

8
00:00:55,716 --> 00:01:02,700
It isn't made from the careless words I said out loud. It is built from the silence I kept.

9
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:08,904
This is the exact weight of the final words I never told my sister before she passed away.

10
00:01:09,204 --> 00:01:14,964
If silence weighs this much, how heavy is an unsaid goodbye?
